	Since every non-empty level subset $(\mu,\mu)_t$ is a subgroup of $\mu_t$, by Theorem \ref{lev_sgp}, $(\mu,\mu)$ is an $L$-subgroup of $\mu$ and hence, $Z_1(\mu)=[\mu,\mu]=(\mu,\mu)$. Next, it can be easily verified that $Z_2(\mu)=[\mu,Z_1(\mu)]$ is given by
	\[ Z_2(\mu)= \begin{cases}
