We now consider the distance of among the $\mu_l^*$, the value of $\mu$ that maximizes $\chi_l$ and $\mu^*=\lim_{l\to\infty} \mu_l^*$. We find numerically that $|\mu_l^*-\mu^*|\propto l^{-1/\nu}$ with $\nu=1$. The scaling of the peak of $\chi_l$ together with the scaling of $\mu_l^*$ suggests that a collapse of the curves may take place, in analogy to statistical thermodynamics results. We find that this is the case indeed, see Fig. \ref{Colapse}
