\subsection{3D plot of Hopf Collapse}

Although the logistic and Chialvo maps are not of the exact canonical form, they can be locally approximated by polynomial maps with identifiable effective nonlinearity $k$. The general susceptibility scaling $\chi_l \sim l^{(3k - 5)/(k - 1)}$ remains valid as long as the local expansion is dominated by a single nonlinear term.



