We study two key fundamental aspects of VQAs in the context of the analog simulators, namely expressivity and the emergence of barren plateau (BP) phenomenon and connect them to the phases of matter. The summary of our fundamental results is illustrated in Fig.~\ref{fig:summary}. In addition, we propose the practical BP-free initialisation strategy based on MBL phase.
