\section{System description and problem formulation}
\label{sec:SysDes}
Consider a hierarchical control system with $N$ local controllers that act on $N$ sub-processes, and a global controller that acts on the LCs. The GC operates at a slower timescale, indexed by $t_1$, while the LCs operate at a faster timescale indexed by $t_0$, with a time scale factor $T$, i.e., $t_0 = Tt_1 + t$, $t = 0,\dots,T-1$, as shown in Fig.~\ref{fig:timeline}(b).

