\section{Limiting behavior}
\label{limibe}

It is fruitful from the theoretical point of view to observe the behavior of the $k$-knot piecewise LRFI when $k \rightarrow \infty $ (see also \cite{Parchami20243583} for the similar results concerning LRFNs).
Then, let us suppose that we are interested in the generation of $\tilde{X}_k = [N(0,1), U(0,1),U(0,1),U(0,2),\Exp(1)]_k$ for the increasing number of the knots~$k$.
After fixing the core and support, we can observe that the left and right arm converged to the reliability functions (for the truncated uniform and exponential cdf, respectively) when $k \rightarrow \infty$ (see Fig.~\ref{ex2hist}).


