    The Hopf RBG link $L(0,*,n)$ is a surgery presentation of the complement of $K_B^{0,n}$ in which $K_B^{0,n}$ is represented by the blue unknot $B$. Thus we can create a surgery diagram of the cyclic $k$-fold branched cover $\Sigma_k(K_B^{0,n})$ of $K_B^{0,n}$ from that surgery presentation by taking the $k$-fold cyclic cover of $L(0,*,n)$ branched along $B$ as shown in the bottom frames of Figure~\ref{fig:dbc}. We do the same for $\Sigma_k(K_G^{0,n})$ in the top frames of Figure \ref{fig:dbc}. 

