\subsection{Inductive formulas for 2, 3, and 4 twists}
For the proof of Proposition \ref{prop:Jipolys} we will need the following inductive formulas, which are all similar to Lemma~\ref{lem:5twist}, but for $2$, $3$, and $4$ twisting strands. 

\begin{lem}\label{lem:2twist_one_up_one_down}
	For $n\in\N_0$, let $K_n$ be the infinite family of knots that are outside of a $3$-ball $B$ identical and inside $B$ have $2$ strands performing $n$-full twists, oriented in opposite directions as shown Figure~\ref{fig:2strands_up_down}. Let $Z$ be the $2$-component link that is outside of $B$ the same as $K_n$ but inside $B$ as shown in Figure~\ref{fig:2strands_up_down}.
	For $n\geq1$, their $F$ polynomials are related by
	\begin{align*}
		F_{K_n}=\,& -F_Z \left(\sum_{k=0}^{n-1}v^{-2k}\right)+ v^{-2n} F_{K_{0}}
		= -F_Z \frac{v^{-2n}-1}{v^{-2}-1}+ v^{-2n} F_{K_{0}}.
	\end{align*}	
\end{lem}

\begin{figure}[t] 
	\centering
	\def\svgwidth{0,4\columnwidth}
