\noindent outputs a Gröbner basis $G$ with $20$ polynomials satisfying that $G \cap \mathbb C[d_1,d_2,d_3,d_4] = \emptyset$ (which means that $J \cap \mathbb C[d_1,d_2,d_3,d_4] = \{0\}$, see, e.g., \cite[Theorem 2 in Chapter 3\S 1]{CLO}), and including the following polynomials:
\begin{itemize}
\item $f_1 =  c_5 (d_1 d_4 - d_2 d_3) + d_1 d_3 d_4 - d_2 d_3 d_4$,
\item $f_2 = c_1 d_4 - c_5 d_2 - d_2 d_4$,
\item $f_3 = b_6 (d_1 d_3 - d_1 d_4) + d_1 d_3 - d_2 d_3$,
