In the process of developing categorical semantics fo classical logic based on LDCs, F\"{u}hrmann and Pym gave a rather useful way to determine whether or not a LDC is mix. 

\begin{lemma}\cite[Lem 3.10]{Fuhrmann_Pym_2007}\label{lem:prove_mix}
A linearly distributive category \bX\ with a map $m\c\bot\rarr\top$ is mix if and only if
\begin{equation}\label{equation_mix_LDC}
    (1_{\bot}\ot m);{u_\ot^R}_{\bot}^{-1} =(m\ot 1_{\bot});{u_\ot^L}_{\bot}^{-1}\c\bot\ot\bot\rarr\bot
\end{equation}
\end{lemma}
