\begin{figure}[H]
\centering
\includegraphics[width=\textwidth]{Figure1.png}
\caption{Data Processing Workflow. This figure outlines the processes of retrospective MRI study
curation. In step (1) all MRI studies evaluating for the presence or absence of brain metastasis
were queried and retrieved from the PACS archive. The EHR was then manually reviewed and
only the studies with evidence of brain metastasis were retained. In step (2), the remaining studies
were processed via a sequence classifier that utilized study metadata. Only T1W, T1CE, T2W, and
FLAIR sequences were included, and other acquired sequences were discarded. In step (3) HD-BET
was used to remove all extra-parenchymal tissue and protect patient privacy. The resulting dataset
was uploaded to TCIA.}
