Amplitude noise in \( |v_r| \) is uniformly sampled from \( [0, \delta v] \), and phase noise in \( \phi_r \) from \( [-\pi, \pi] \).  
Results are obtained via Monte Carlo sampling with 1000 realizations, using \( |v_r| = 0.5 \), \( |v_{cr}| = 1 \), and \( \phi_r = \phi_{cr} = 0 \).  
Both observables remain robust against arbitrary phase noise in \( \phi_r \) and amplitude noise for \( \delta v \le |v_{cr}| - |v_r| \).
}
