$\3\1\bar{\2}, \3\1\2, \2\1\bar{\1}, \e\1\2, \e\1\bar{\1}, 
\e\1\e'$ of {\bf BG3}(b), where $\e\succ \e'$ and both are in $\cal E$.

\item {\bf Type U.} As shown in Fig. \ref{fig:BG}(3.1)-(3.3), this type of leading term 
