   (b) The coupling between positive and negative frequencies in the scattered intensity is given in the final term of Eq. (\ref{eq:interference}) and is proportional to the product, $\left|\widetilde{s}\left( \omega_{\rm out}-\omega_{\rm in}\right)\widetilde{s}\left( - \omega_{\rm out}-\omega_{\rm in} \right)\right|$ (shown in orange).  We can obtain this product by taking the blue region in panel a and multiplying it with its copy, flipped across the $x$--axis  (shown in grey).  In this example, the input frequencies $\pm\omega_{\rm in}$ lie outside the orange region, and thus negligible phase-sensitivity is expected.
