The SDSS/WISE offset criterion results in a parent sample of 356 merger systems with red mid-IR colors and one or more SDSS/WISE offsets. Our target selection methodology is summarized in Figure~\ref{flowchart}. We then selected 37 targets with nearby guide stars for follow-up high resolution Adaptive Optics (AO) NIRC2 imaging at the Keck observatory. We also included 11 targets with publicly available NIRC2 imaging in the Keck archive (see Table \ref{table:archivesample}), resulting in a sample of 48 galaxy mergers with Keck AO imaging (see Table \ref{table:sampleproperties}). With this imaging data we search for evidence of previously unresolved substructure and/or closely separated nuclei in these late-stage mergers.



