Galaxies in our sample are classified as AGNs or star-forming (SF) galaxies based on their optical narrow emission line ratios, using the Baldwin-Philips-Terlevich diagram \citep[BPT;][]{Baldwin+1981}. Classifications follow the criteria of \citet[$K_{03}$]{kauffmann+2003a}, \citet[$K_{01}$]{kewley+2001}, and \citet[$S_{06}$]{stasinska+2006} applied to emission line fluxes from the MPA-JHU DR8 Catalog \citep{kauffmann+2003b,brinchmann+2004,tremonti+2004}. Only spectra with signal-to-noise ratios greater than 5 in the relevant narrow lines are classified with the BPT diagram. We also use the three-band AGN color cut from \cite{jarrett+2011} to identify MIR AGNs in the sample.

