Our goal in this work is to determine if our adopted pre-selection strategy, searching for advanced red mergers with significant SDSS/WISE offsets, is successful in identifying unresolved substructure in which one or more AGNs may reside. Unfortunately, archival NIRC2 data is limited, preventing a large statistical analysis. Nonetheless, we constructed two comparison samples to assess whether our success in detecting substructure is enhanced by the SDSS/WISE offset selection or if it is primarily due to the fact we are selecting late-stage mergers.
