\subsection{Quantum mutual information lifetime}

Taking into account the measurement-conditioned state $\ket{\psi_\bfz}_{RA_t}$ and unconditioned state $\rho_{RA_t}$ at time step $t$, we quantify the information shared by parties $R$ and $A_t$ via QMI. 
Given a measurement trajectory $\bfz$, the quantum information retained in $A_t$ at time step $t$ is quantified by the {\it measurement-conditioned QMI} defined as:
\be 
% I(R:A_t|Z)=\E_{\bfz} I(R:A_t|\bfz)_{\psi(\bfz;\bm U)},
\overline{I(R:A_t|\bfz)} \equiv \E_{\bfz} I(R:A_t|\bfz),
\label{QMI_cond}
\ee 
where $\E_\bfz$ denotes averaging over the different measurement outcomes according to the outcome probabilities $P_{\bm U}(\bfz)$, and $I(R:A_t|\bfz)$ is the QMI of the conditional state $\ket{\psi_{\bfz}}_{RA_t}$ in Eq.~\eqref{state_RAt}. 
For the unconditional dynamics, the {\it measurement-unconditioned QMI} 
\be
    I(R:A_t) \equiv S(\rho_R) + S(\rho_{A_t}) - S(\rho_{RA_t}),
    \label{eq:uncond_MI}
\ee
is thus evaluated on $\rho_{RA_t}$ in Eq.~\eqref{unconditional_dynamics}, where $\rho_R, \rho_{A_t}$ are the reduced states on corresponding subsystem $R, A_t$. 

