\section{Kuznyechik Block Cipher: Technical Specification: GOST R 34.12-2015}


Kuznyechik is a symmetric block cipher standardized as GOST R 34.12-2015, serving as the official encryption standard of the Russian Federation. The cipher operates on 128-bit blocks with a 256-bit key, employing a substitution-permutation network (SPN) structure over 9 rounds, plus a key whitening at the backend.
The cipher operates over the finite field $\mathbb{F}_{2^8}$ with the irreducible polynomial $p(x) = x^8 + x^7 + x^6 + x + 1$. Each 128-bit block is treated as a vector of 16 bytes (elements of $\mathbb{F}_{2^8}$).

